  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read both issues, task 203's notes and the entry points; inventory existing cached sources of column display names and option labels; decide and record the source (with the §11 answers) in notes/task-210-notes.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Failing tests first (describer column names and statuscode labels with fallback; authorable-column label guard; rule wizard display text with logical values).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the server label source and describer change; then the client display text.</step>
    <step order="4">Filtered tests (Signals incl. baselines, OntologyAdmin, RuleBodyDescriber), full ArchTests, BFF build, publish-size delta; client tests, typecheck, client-lint.</step>
    <step order="5">PR to master, body "Closes #3040, Closes #3020"; notes in notes/task-210-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The plain-language line names every authorable column by a display label (guard test over the allow-list) and a statuscode test by its option label when known, by number otherwise; the formal line is unchanged; tests fail on origin/master.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The rule wizard's column list and "Values the message can quote" show display names; the selected value and the stored rule body keep the logical name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No per-request metadata read on the decision path (test or code-level proof); a metadata failure falls back to logical name / number without failing the request.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Contract baselines updated in the PR; build, filtered tests, full ArchTests, client tests, typecheck and client-lint pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Main session checks the rule wizard and a decision's "How this was determined" on dev after the next uac-r2 dev BFF build and the Console auto-deploy.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix needs a schema change, a change to stored rule bodies or the allow-list, a per-request metadata read, or a change to the describer's callers' behaviour beyond the shown text: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree (C:\wt210); PR to master.</protocol>
